:true,"x":44,"y":499}],"portalColor":{"OT":"#8C93AD","NT":"#D8DCEB"},"groups":[{"label":"Creation","color":"#7FB77E"},{"label":"Noah","color":"#4EA8DE"},{"label":"Abraham","color":"#D9A441"},{"label":"Moses","color":"#C05746"},{"label":"David","color":"#B07CD4"},{"label":"New covenant","color":"#E4DFCE"},{"label":"Unassigned","color":"#5A6178"}],"relkinds":[{"key":"quoted-in","label":"Quoted in","color":"#E8C15A","strong":true},{"key":"fulfilled-in","label":"Fulfilled in","color":"#D9715C","strong":true},{"key":"parallels","label":"Parallels","color":"#6E9BD1","strong":false},{"key":"illustrates-doctrine","label":"Illustrates doctrine","color":"#9B8AD1","strong":false},{"key":"part-of-covenant","label":"Part of covenant","color":"#5FBFA0","strong":false}],"counts":{"topics":7,"portals":1,"edges":7,"relations":0,"outbound":0},"nodes":[{"id":"bt_book_tit","p":0,"x":56,"y":109,"s":-1,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"Titus: overview","d":"Paul's letter to Titus in Crete about appointing elders, opposing unruly teachers, sound doctrine in daily life, and salvation by grace that leads to good works.","q":"Can {{name}} explain in a few sentences what Titus is about?","ev":["Describe the three chapters: order and elders (1), sound doctrine and grace (2), mercy and good works (3)"],"pp":[[55,1,1,16],[55,2,1,15],[55,3,1,15]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_elders_crete","p":0,"x":56,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"THEME","t":"Elders in every city of Crete","d":"Paul greets Titus, mentions the hope of eternal life promised before the world began, and tells him he left him in Crete to appoint elders who are blameless and hold fast the faithful word.","q":"Can {{name}} explain why Paul left Titus in Crete and what kind of men were to be elders (1:5-9)?","ev":["State why Paul left Titus in Crete (1:5)","List some qualities of an elder in 1:6-9"],"pp":[[55,1,1,9]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_rebuke_deceivers","p":0,"x":244,"y":239,"s":0,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"THEME","t":"Rebuking the unruly teachers","d":"Many unruly talkers, especially of the circumcision, subvert households for gain; Titus is to rebuke them sharply, since they profess to know God but deny him by their works.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Paul says about those who profess to know God but deny him by works (1:16)?","ev":["Say what these teachers do (1:11)","Explain 1:16"],"pp":[[55,1,10,16]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_sound_doctrine_lives","p":0,"x":56,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"THEME","t":"Sound doctrine in every household","d":"Titus is to teach what fits sound doctrine to older men and women, younger women and men, and servants, and to be a pattern of good works himself.","q":"Can {{name}} describe how Paul wants the different groups to live and why (2:5, 2:8, 2:10)?","ev":["Name the groups in 2:2-10","State why Titus must be an example (2:7-8)"],"pp":[[55,2,1,10]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_grace_appeared","p":0,"x":244,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"The grace of God has appeared","d":"The grace of God that brings salvation has appeared to all men, teaching us to deny ungodliness and live soberly while looking for the glorious appearing of our great God and Saviour Jesus Christ, who gave himself to redeem and purify a people for himself.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Titus 2:11-14 says grace teaches us and what Christ did for us?","ev":["Say what grace teaches in 2:12","State what Christ gave himself to do in 2:14"],"pp":[[55,2,11,15]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_saved_by_mercy","p":0,"x":432,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"DOCTRINE","t":"Saved by mercy, not by works","d":"Believers once lived in folly and malice, but God our Saviour saved them according to his mercy, not works, through the washing of regeneration and renewing of the Holy Ghost, that they might be justified by grace and be heirs; they are to be careful to maintain good works.","q":"Can {{name}} explain what Titus 3:4-7 says about how God saved us?","ev":["Say what 3:5 says saved us and what it says did not","Describe how believers are to treat others (3:1-2)"],"pp":[[55,3,1,8]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_tit_closing_warnings","p":0,"x":620,"y":369,"s":1,"g":6,"bk":"TIT","ty":"THEME","t":"Avoiding division, and final instructions","d":"Titus is to avoid foolish questions and genealogies, reject a divisive man after two admonitions, and Paul closes with travel instructions, names of helpers and greetings.","q":"Can {{name}} tell what Paul says to avoid and what to do after admonishing a divisive person twice (3:9-10)?","ev":["State what to do with a divisive man (3:10)","Name people mentioned in 3:12-13"],"pp":[[55,3,9,15]],"tier":null},{"id":"bt_book_1ti","p":1,"x":244,"y":499,"s":-2,"g":6,"bk":"1TI","ty":"BOOK_OVERVIEW","t":"1 Timothy: overview","d":"Paul's letter to Timothy at Ephesus about sound doctrine, prayer, order in the church, qualified leaders, and a minister's conduct and charge.","q":"Can {{name}} explain in a few sentences what 1 Timothy is about (see 3:14-15)?","ev":["Describe how 3:15 states the letter's purpose","Name the main sections: false teaching, prayer and conduct, leaders, Timothy's ministry, groups in the church, closing charge"],"pp":[[53,1,1,20],[53,2,1,15],[53,3,1,16],[53,4,1,16],[53,5,1,25],[53,6,1,21]],"tier":null}],"edges":[[2,1,1],[3,2,0],[4,3,1],[5,4,0],[6,5,0],[0,1,0],[1,7,0]],"rel":[]}
